{**
 * c-preference-switcher - every preference this build has, each drawn as the
 * set of answers somebody can switch between.
 *
 * One component for every place the switch appears - the top of the style
 * guide, and the menu of whoever is signed in to the administration - so that
 * there is one switch to keep right rather than two to keep alike.
 *
 * Nothing is listed here. The preferences and their answers come out of
 * Trilobit\Core\Preference\PreferenceCatalogue by way of
 * Preferences::offered(), and the words on the controls are derived from the
 * names, so a fourth preference is an entry in the catalogue and not a line in
 * this file. tests/Template/PreferenceSwitcherOffersEveryPreferenceTest fails
 * when what is drawn and what the catalogue has part company in either
 * direction.
 *
 * A control says which preference it sets and to what, and nothing else:
 * assets/app.ts moves the attribute on <html> and tells the server. **Which
 * control is the chosen one is said once, in aria-pressed.** It was said twice
 * until 2026-09-09 - as the attribute and as the button's variant - and the
 * script only ever moved the attribute, so clicking another theme repainted the
 * page and left the mark on the theme that was no longer on. The variant is
 * therefore fixed and assets/base.css draws .c-button[aria-pressed='true'] as
 * the one in force.
 *
 * It is preferred() and not value() that decides which control is pressed: the
 * switch shows the person's own setting, which is not always what the page it
 * happens to be on is drawn at - see Trilobit\Core\Preference\Preferences.
 *}

{import 'button.latte'}

{define preferenceSwitcher, Trilobit\Core\Preference\Preferences $preferences, ?string $testId = null}
    <div class="c-preference-switcher" data-testid="{$testId}">
        {foreach $preferences->offered() as $name => $preference}
            {var string $label = ($name|replace: '-', ' '|firstUpper)}

            <div class="c-preference-switcher__group" role="group" aria-label="{$label}">
                <span class="c-preference-switcher__label" aria-hidden="true">{$label}</span>

                {foreach $preference->values as $value}
                    {include button,
                        label: ($value|firstUpper),
                        variant: 'quiet',
                        testId: $name . '-choice-' . $value,
                        attributes: [
                            'data-preference' => $name,
                            'data-preference-value' => $value,
                            'aria-pressed' => $value === $preferences->preferred($name) ? 'true' : 'false',
                        ]}
                {/foreach}
            </div>
        {/foreach}
    </div>
{/define}
